.Dd July 11, 2022
.Dt ZPOOL-LABELCLEAR 8
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm zpool-labelclear
.Nd remove ZFS label information from device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm zpool
.Cm labelclear
.Op Fl f
.Ar device
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Removes ZFS label information from the specified
.Ar device .
If the
.Ar device
is a cache device, it also removes the L2ARC header
(persistent L2ARC).
The
.Ar device
must not be part of an active pool configuration.
.Pp
This overwrites pool metadata, making all data on the
.Ar device
inaccessible without specialized recovery tools.
Unlike
.Nm zpool Cm destroy ,
this cannot be undone by ZFS tooling.
Only use this when you don't care about the data on the
.Ar device .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f
Treat exported or foreign devices as inactive.
.El
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zpool-destroy 8 ,
.Xr zpool-detach 8 ,
.Xr zpool-remove 8 ,
.Xr zpool-replace 8
